316 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 193 0 R
/E (The AgriDrone AI system improves the efficiency of farming by using drones to monitor and assess land conditions and crop health. This technology addresses major agricultural problems such as delayed identification of crop diseases, inadequate monitoring of fields, and reliance on manual inspection. AgriDrone AI uses aerial imagery combined with machine learning to provide quicker, more precise, and data-driven evaluations of crop health and land condition, resulting in increased production and decreased waste of resources.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
317 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 193 0 R
/E (The AgriDrone AI system consists of a manually operated quadcopter drone with a camera used to photograph agricultural fields. These pictures serve as the primary source of information when analyzing and evaluating agricultural fields. This approach differs from a fully automated system in that it offers reliability and cost savings due to the use of human-operated flight combined with automated data processing. The photos taken by the drone are sent to an online system for processing using advanced computer vision and deep learning techniques.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
318 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 193 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
319 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 193 0 R
/E (The second pipeline is concerned with detecting field boundaries and providing land segmentation. By using a deep learning edge detection model such as DexiNed, the boundaries between different sections of farmland can be identified using aerial imagery. Once the boundaries have been identified, segmentation techniques will also be applied in order to segment the overall field into smaller plots. After the segmentation has been completed, geometric calculations will be performed to calculate the area of each of the segmented plots from the first step, which can provide valuable insights into land management, crop planning and resource allocation. This will reduce the number of surveys that need to be done manually and improve the accuracy of field analysis.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
320 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 193 0 R
/E (The overall system is built upon a modern web-based platform that provides the user interface for interacting with and visualizing the system. The frontend is built using technologies such as Next.js and React, which provide functionality for uploading images, performing live detection, visualizing boundaries, and providing analytical dashboards. The backend is implemented with FastAPI, which allows for communication between the machine learning models and provides for efficient processing of tasks. A PostgreSQL database is used to store the metadata related to fields, detections, and outputs from the system, allowing for a historical record of actions completed as well as insights based on data.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
321 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/P 194 0 R
/Pg 16 0 R
/A [1098 0 R 0]
/K [0]
>>
endobj
322 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 194 0 R
/E (2 )
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
323 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 194 0 R
/T (AgriDrone AI has many advantages, such as lessening the amount of time needed for agricultural work, speeding up the process of analyzing large areas of agriculture, and increasing the accuracy of identifying crop disease and the boundaries of fields. That would also provide farmers and other stakeholders with real-time data and analysis in order to make better decisions about their crops and other agricultural products, which is part of precision agriculture. While the current system uses manual aerial imagery processed through drones, it is designed to be scalable, allowing for future implementation of features like autonomous drone navigation, video analysis in real-time, Internet of Things \(IoT\)-based environmental monitoring through sensors embedded in various pieces of equipment, and predictive data models.)
/E (AgriDrone AI has many advantages, such as lessening the amount of time needed for agricultural work, speeding up the process of analyzing large areas of agriculture, and increasing the accuracy of identifying crop disease and the boundaries of fields. That would also provide farmers and other stakeholders with real-time data and analysis in order to make better decisions about their crops and other agricultural products, which is part of precision agriculture. While the current system uses manual aerial imagery processed through drones, it is designed to be scalable, allowing for future implementation of features like autonomous drone navigation, video analysis in real-time, Internet of Things \(IoT\)-based environmental monitoring through sensors embedded in various pieces of equipment, and predictive data models.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
324 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 194 0 R
/T (In conclusion, AgriDrone AI is a smart agricultural approach that includes data acquisition through drones, data analysis conducted through artificial intelligence, and digital/user-friendly interfaces that help improve how agriculture is monitored today and provide the basis for future development of smart agriculture solutions, leading to improved productivity, sustainable production methods, and a more resilient agriculture industry.)
/E (In conclusion, AgriDrone AI is a smart agricultural approach that includes data acquisition through drones, data analysis conducted through artificial intelligence, and digital/user-friendly interfaces that help improve how agriculture is monitored today and provide the basis for future development of smart agriculture solutions, leading to improved productivity, sustainable production methods, and a more resilient agriculture industry.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
325 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/P 195 0 R
/Pg 17 0 R
/A [1099 0 R 0]
/K [0]
>>
endobj
326 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 195 0 R
/T (INTRODUCTION )
/E (INTRODUCTION )
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
327 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 195 0 R
/E (3)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
328 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 195 0 R
/E (The AgriDrone AI is an advanced agriculture monitor that implements drone technology, A.I. and data-informed decision making tools for modernisation of agri-businesses and traditional agri-practices. Agriculture has been and will undoubtedly continue to be one of the world's top industries providing employment and food security for billions of people around the world. To date, agriculture has continued to face major challenges including, but not limited to, delayed diagnoses of crop health issues, ineffective management of farms/plants/crops, unequal access to all resources, and a heavy reliance on manual labour. These limitations have led to reduced crop yields/production, higher operating expenses, and lengthy time frames to respond to issues affecting crop production. The AgriDrone AI programme will address the aforementioned challenges in agriculture by providing an intelligent, solicitous, and technology-oriented alternative to how we currently monitor, manage, and thereby, overcome challenges related to agricultural production.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
329 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 195 0 R
/E (The system uses a semi-automated method with human control of the drone for aerial photos of agriculture. This provides a simple, low-cost, dependable solution in cases where a fully autonomous drone is not possible due to regulations, technology, or cost restraints. The drone is used as a source of data collection through a camera, taking high-resolution images from different heights and angles of the crops and field in order to perform extensive analyses of crop conditions and land characteristics through image analysis rather than visiting the field.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
330 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 195 0 R
/E (A powerful artificial intelligence framework is at the core of AgriDrone AI - it processes captured images using two main analysis pipelines: the plant disease detection pipeline detects plant health problems at an early stage with the use of deep learning and computer vision techniques. The plant disease detection pipeline uses an object detection model based on YOLO \(You Only Look Once\) to locate and separate the leaf area in an image. This step is important since this helps to filter out irrelevant data such as the ground, the sky or surrounding objects, and ensures that only useful data on the plants is included in the analysis. After this has occurred the regions identified are validated with HSV-based filtering to ensure they represent vegetation and further minimise the number of false positives.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
331 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 195 0 R
/E (The original content has been paraphrased with the intent of making it consistent with the intent of the original writing. )
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
332 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 195 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
333 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 195 0 R
/E (After pre-processing the images, the resulting image is passed through a convolutional neural network \(CNN\) that has been trained on a number of plant disease datasets. Each image is classified by the CNN into either a healthy or a diseased condition, along with a confidence score that indicates how confident the model is about its prediction. This type of automated classifier will allow fast and early detection of diseases, thus enabling growers to take action to prevent the spreading of disease throughout the entire field before they establish themselves in larger numbers.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
334 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /Figure
/P 196 0 R
/Pg 18 0 R
/A [1100 0 R 0]
/K [0]
>>
endobj
335 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 196 0 R
/T (The second area of focus for this system is the detection of field boundaries and segmentation of the different parts of agricultural fields. There are many times that an agriculture field is split up into various different areas \(plots\) that all have different uses, but all relate to agriculture, such as rotational crops, irrigation systems, or test plots. It takes a lot of time and is very hard to identify and measure these plots manually. To identify and measure the field boundary, the AgriDrone AI system uses edge detection technologies with advanced models including DexiNed, to detect where the boundaries of differing regions are located in an aerial image. Once the boundary has been detected, the images of the boundaries will be viewed and processed using segmentation algorithms to break up the entire field into individual plots. Using geometric calculations the system will provide an estimation of the area of each plot to allow for accurate measurements of the plots that can be used for planning and monitoring and optimization of the agricultural activity.)
/E (The second area of focus for this system is the detection of field boundaries and segmentation of the different parts of agricultural fields. There are many times that an agriculture field is split up into various different areas \(plots\) that all have different uses, but all relate to agriculture, such as rotational crops, irrigation systems, or test plots. It takes a lot of time and is very hard to identify and measure these plots manually. To identify and measure the field boundary, the AgriDrone AI system uses edge detection technologies with advanced models including DexiNed, to detect where the boundaries of differing regions are located in an aerial image. Once the boundary has been detected, the images of the boundaries will be viewed and processed using segmentation algorithms to break up the entire field into individual plots. Using geometric calculations the system will provide an estimation of the area of each plot to allow for accurate measurements of the plots that can be used for planning and monitoring and optimization of the agricultural activity.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
