/P 200 0 R
/T (Tm et al. [11] demonstrated a CNN-SVM hybrid architecture achieving 95.48% accuracy on a rice disease dataset, highlighting that combining deep feature extraction with classical classification heads can yield competitive accuracy on small, domain-specific datasets where pure end-to-end CNNs may overfit. This finding is relevant to the PlantDiseaseCNN component of AgriDrone, which employs transfer learning from an ImageNet-pretrained backbone to compensate for limited labeled agricultural training data in field collection scenarios.)
/E (Tm et al. [11] demonstrated a CNN-SVM hybrid architecture achieving 95.48% accuracy on a rice disease dataset, highlighting that combining deep feature extraction with classical classification heads can yield competitive accuracy on small, domain-specific datasets where pure end-to-end CNNs may overfit. This finding is relevant to the PlantDiseaseCNN component of AgriDrone, which employs transfer learning from an ImageNet-pretrained backbone to compensate for limited labeled agricultural training data in field collection scenarios.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
372 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 200 0 R
/T (Rangarajan et al. [12] applied AlexNet and VGG16 transfer learning to tomato disease classification, achieving 91.2% accuracy and demonstrating that deeper pre-trained architectures provide diminishing returns beyond VGG-depth for single-crop disease classification tasks. The DexiNed component of the AgriDrone AI pipeline serves a fundamentally different function from disease classification: it performs dense edge detection for field boundary delineation in the aerial imagery, enabling the system to segment treatment zones and calculate affected area in square meters for the plant_detections schema's affected_area_sqm field.)
/E (Rangarajan et al. [12] applied AlexNet and VGG16 transfer learning to tomato disease classification, achieving 91.2% accuracy and demonstrating that deeper pre-trained architectures provide diminishing returns beyond VGG-depth for single-crop disease classification tasks. The DexiNed component of the AgriDrone AI pipeline serves a fundamentally different function from disease classification: it performs dense edge detection for field boundary delineation in the aerial imagery, enabling the system to segment treatment zones and calculate affected area in square meters for the plant_detections schema's affected_area_sqm field.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
373 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 200 0 R
/T (DeChant et al. [13] achieved 96.7% classification accuracy for Northern Leaf Blight on in-field maize imagery using a custom CNN, representing one of the strongest validations of CNN-based disease detection in true field conditions rather than controlled settings. Their work was limited, however, to a single disease and single crop type, with no cloud deployment infrastructure. The AgriDrone AI platform targets multi-crop, multi-disease generalization through its modular model architecture, where the YOLO leaf detector and disease classifier can be independently retrained and hot-swapped via the Python FastAPI model management layer without interrupting the frontend dashboard or database services.)
/E (DeChant et al. [13] achieved 96.7% classification accuracy for Northern Leaf Blight on in-field maize imagery using a custom CNN, representing one of the strongest validations of CNN-based disease detection in true field conditions rather than controlled settings. Their work was limited, however, to a single disease and single crop type, with no cloud deployment infrastructure. The AgriDrone AI platform targets multi-crop, multi-disease generalization through its modular model architecture, where the YOLO leaf detector and disease classifier can be independently retrained and hot-swapped via the Python FastAPI model management layer without interrupting the frontend dashboard or database services.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [6]
