/E (Thenmozhi and Rajesh [10] demonstrated a cloud-hosted REST inference architecture for plant disease detection, achieving 90.2% accuracy and 3-second end-to-end latency using MobileNet served via a REST API. Their work validates the cloud REST inference model adopted by AgriDrone AI but was limited to a single-model, single-endpoint architecture without fleet management, mission planning, or persistent geospatial storage. The AgriDrone AI API layer, built on Next.js Route Handlers, exposes eleven distinct endpoint groups covering drones, fields, flights, missions, alerts, detections, sensor data, plant detection, boundary detection, dashboard statistics, and AI inference, forming a comprehensive data orchestration layer between the drone hardware and the cloud database.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [5]
>>
