/P 205 0 R
/E (Agricultural monitoring practices are manual and inefficient, do not provide a high degree of accuracy in their results and do not scale to meet the demands of today's farms. Farmers frequently visually inspect their crops for signs of disease and to assess the condition of their fields; this is a time-consuming and error-prone method of assessing both the overall health of a crop/field and its specific needs as the area of land being farmed continues to grow larger.)
/Pg 27 0 R
