/E (Field boundary detection is still an area where farming remains difficult. Using traditional methods to measure land can be time-consuming, and these methods will not provide a clear separation of the plots. In addition, with boundaries that lack definition, it can be even more difficult to separate fields. Current automated solutions can struggle with complicated field structures, overlapping crops, or complex image contrast between fields and crop types.)
/Pg 27 0 R
