/P 1154 0 R
/E (Leaf Recognition via YOLO)
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
503 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 211 0 R
/T (The first step of the pipeline will be the identification of leaf areas within the input image using a YOLO \(You Only Look Once\) Object Detection Model. By using the provided bounding boxes for leaf areas, the model isolates all other regions of interest that may appear in the input image \(e.g., dirt, clouds, etc.\) to focus solely on the leaf areas present.)
/E (The first step of the pipeline will be the identification of leaf areas within the input image using a YOLO \(You Only Look Once\) Object Detection Model. By using the provided bounding boxes for leaf areas, the model isolates all other regions of interest that may appear in the input image \(e.g., dirt, clouds, etc.\) to focus solely on the leaf areas present.)
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
504 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 1155 0 R
/E (HSV Validation)
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
505 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 211 0 R
/T (After recognizing the leaf areas, the next step will include applying HSV \(Hue, Saturation and Value\) Color Filtering to confirm that the identified leaf areas are indeed vegetation. This helps to remove non-plant items from future analysis to create an even more accurate measurement for detecting the presence of leaf areas.)
/E (After recognizing the leaf areas, the next step will include applying HSV \(Hue, Saturation and Value\) Color Filtering to confirm that the identified leaf areas are indeed vegetation. This helps to remove non-plant items from future analysis to create an even more accurate measurement for detecting the presence of leaf areas.)
/Pg 33 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
