638 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 218 0 R
/E (The AgriDrone AI System's disease detection module is shown in Figure 5.2. This module uses an aerial or close-up photo of a crop leaf to diagnose any possible disease on that leaf. An AI pipeline takes the image uploaded by the user and passes it through a trained model, which outputs sick parts of the crop and overall condition of the crop. )
/Pg 40 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
639 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 218 0 R
/E (The diagnosed image will be the most apparent part of the user interface, and other pieces of diagnosis information \(e.g., confidence levels that the disease has been detected and a classification of the crop's condition\) will be included in the interface for the user. When a confidence score \(> 80%\) is shown, it tells the user how likely it is that the disease was correctly identified when combined with visual cues, such as colored labels and warning sections, showing the difference between diseased and healthy output. )
/Pg 40 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
640 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 218 0 R
/E (The system will also have a summary of the problems provided below the image with severity levels. The data for the problems detected will be produced using a YOLO-based detection model and a CNN classifier to ensure that crop diseases are detected and accurately identified in both locations and classifications. As shown in this interface, the AgriDrone AI System can give users fast, understandable feedback on detecting diseases before they can spread. This will aid the user in intervening with pesticides as soon as possible.)
/Pg 40 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
