/T (6.1 CONCLUSION)
/E (6.1 CONCLUSION)
/Pg 48 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
733 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 226 0 R
/E (AgriDrone AI provides a practical and efficient way to modernize the monitoring of agriculture through drone technology, artificial intelligence \(AI\), and web-based systems. This project successfully shows that combining aerial data acquisition with the latest advances in machine learning will allow us to analyze both crop health and field structure with increased accuracy and efficiency. Instead of relying solely on traditional means of manually inspecting crops, we provide a better alternative by using a drone operated manually to capture images of the crops and then applying AI based pipelines to detect disease and to segment boundaries in a field. )
/Pg 48 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
734 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 226 0 R
/E (Using object detection to identify disease in plants and deep learning to classify diseases in plants allows us to identify potential problems with crop health before they become major problems, and therefore reduce the likelihood of crop loss and increase yield. Similarly, using an accurate field boundary detection and segmentation module gives us information regarding land distribution and area for each plot to enable more informed resource management and planning activities. By consolidating these functions into a single platform, we have significantly improved the overall usability and functionality of the system.)
/Pg 48 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
735 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 226 0 R
/E (The system is further strengthened by its full-stack architecture, which includes a responsive frontend interface, a robust backend for processing and API management, and a structured database for data storage and retrieval. This ensures smooth communication between components and allows users to interact with the system easily while accessing meaningful insights. The modular design also makes the system scalable and adaptable for future improvements.)
/Pg 48 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
736 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 226 0 R
/E (Although the current system operates with manual drone control and image-based analysis, it lays a strong foundation for future advancements such as autonomous drone navigation, real-time video processing, IoT-based environmental monitoring, and predictive analytics. These enhancements can further improve system capabilities and expand its applicability in precision agriculture.)
/Pg 48 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
737 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 226 0 R
/E (In conclusion, AgriDrone AI bridges the gap between traditional farming practices and modern technological solutions by providing a data-driven approach to agricultural monitoring. It enhances efficiency, supports informed decision-making, and contributes to the development of smarter and more sustainable farming systems capable of meeting future agricultural demands.)
/Pg 48 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
