2232 0 obj
<<
/Title (Ferentinos et al. [9] extended the CNN plant disease classification paradigm to drone-captured imagery, achieving 96.3% accuracy on a curated aerial leaf dataset. Their work confirmed that CNN architectures can generalize to aerial perspectives but operated in offline batch-processing mode without cloud deployment. The AgriDrone AI platform addresses this deployment gap by pairing YOLO-based leaf detection with a PlantDiseaseCNN classifier, both served as microservices through a Python FastAPI backend. The YOLO detection stage isolates leaf regions-of-interest from the full aerial frame before passing them to the classifier, substantially reducing the false positive rate caused by soil patches, water bodies, and background vegetation that contaminate raw frame classification.)
/Dest [22 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 2226 0 R
/Next 2238 0 R
>>
endobj
